{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brickred-hapless-dromedary","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nAgents sometimes botch the `rebar-ticket:` trailer, leaving a ticket's change unlinkable at close time. The `COMMITS` event type and `attach_commits` reducer already exist (used by the code-review workflow) — what is missing is an author-facing repair surface and a consumer. Approved design (analysis ticket b902-18af-14ed-4da1): expose retroactive commit linking on ALL THREE surfaces (CLI, Python library, MCP), document it clearly, and then add a cheap deterministic close-gate check that the linked change's diff is consistent with the recorded file_impact. Explicitly OUT of scope: using the linked commits as a completion-verifier diff basis — linked commits may be incomplete even when they match file_impact, and CV already prefetches from file_impact.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. CLI verb `rebar attach-commits <ticket> <sha>...` wrapping the existing `rebar.attach_commits` seam (validate each SHA resolves in the repo; union-add semantics unchanged).\n2. Library re-export (`rebar.attach_commits` already importable — confirm and document) and MCP tool (`attach_commits`) with outputSchema, following the existing write-tool pattern.\n3. DET close check: when a ticket records `file_impact` AND linked/referencing commits are found, compare the union of those commits' changed paths against the recorded file_impact; a changed path outside the declared impact (allowing tests/docs conventions per existing gate rules) is a deterministic close BLOCK naming the mismatched paths. No LLM.\n4. Documentation: `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, and the commit-trailer guide (`rebar explain commit-trailer` source) each name the repair verb and when to use it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar attach-commits <ticket> <sha>` records a COMMITS event and `rebar show` reflects it; invalid SHAs are rejected with a clear error. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"attach_commits\" -x` passes.\n- [ ] The MCP server exposes `attach_commits` with an outputSchema and the Python library documents the call; both route through the same seam as the CLI. Verify: MCP tool-inventory test updated and passing.\n- [ ] With file_impact recorded and linked commits present, a commit touching a path outside the declared impact deterministically blocks close with the offending paths named; a conforming diff does not block. Verify: unit tests cover both directions.\n- [ ] The three docs name the verb and the repair workflow. Verify: grep assertions in the docs test tier.","id":"cec6-0a0e-38a9-4234","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"attach-commits repair verb on all three surfaces + DET file-impact-vs-diff close check"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786486370906382001,"uuid":"d043bf71-30bd-4e3e-bc0b-02cae6cdaffb"}